{# Register timeline — twelve months as marks on a rule.
   Expects:
     pulse           — array from the pulseMonths filter (12 slots)
     pulseCurrentKey — 'yyyy-MM' of the current post, if any (marks its month)

   Every month since the first post is rendered. The track scrolls
   horizontally with the scrollbar hidden, starting at the most recent end;
   how many months are on screen follows the container width rather than a
   breakpoint.

   Plain HTML and CSS, no SVG and no JavaScript: each month with entries is
   an <a>, so it gets a native tooltip on hover and goes somewhere on click.
   Empty months are a bare tick, not a link.

   Encoding: mark size is scaled by AREA (side = 4 x sqrt(count), capped),
   because sizing by side length would make a busy month look four times
   heavier rather than twice. These marks are the one deliberate exception
   to the site's no-radius rule: a circle reads as a point in time where a
   square reads as a bar. See .kh-timeline in _kh-dataviz.scss.

   Type is deliberately NOT encoded here. The strip this replaced stacked
   article/digest/impact ticks, which made it read as a chart to study
   rather than an ambient stamp. Counts by type stay in the tooltip. #}
{%- if pulse and pulse.length -%}
{#- 35-odd month links sit between the skip link and the page content, so
    the strip needs its own bypass or keyboard users tab through the whole
    archive to reach the first heading. -#}
<a class="kh-u-sr-only kh-skip-link" href="#kh-after-timeline">Skip publishing timeline</a>
<nav class="kh-timeline" aria-label="Publishing timeline" data-pagefind-ignore>
  {#- No visible label: the marks are meant to be noticed and worked out,
     not announced. The text stays for assistive tech and the CSS-off view. -#}
  <p class="kh-u-sr-only">Entries published each month since the first post.</p>
  <ol class="kh-timeline__track">
    {%- for m in pulse %}
    {%- if m.gap %}
    {#- A run of years with nothing published, collapsed to one break rather
        than scrolled through. Caption comes from _data/timelineGaps.json. -#}
    <li class="kh-timeline__slot kh-timeline__slot--gap" title="{{ m.label }}{% if m.caption %} — {{ m.caption }}{% else %} — no entries{% endif %}">
      <span class="kh-timeline__break" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="kh-timeline__year kh-timeline__year--gap" aria-hidden="true">{{ m.label }}</span>
      <span class="kh-u-sr-only">{{ m.label }}: no entries.{% if m.caption %} {{ m.caption }}{% endif %}</span>
    </li>
    {%- else %}
    {%- set tip = m.longLabel ~ ' — ' ~ m.total ~ (' entry' if m.total == 1 else ' entries') %}
    <li class="kh-timeline__slot{% if m.yearStart %} kh-timeline__slot--year{% endif %}{% if pulseCurrentKey and m.key == pulseCurrentKey %} kh-timeline__slot--current{% endif %}" data-year="{{ m.year }}">
      {%- if m.total and m.url %}
      <a class="kh-timeline__mark" href="{{ m.url | url }}" style="--kh-mark-size: {{ m.size }}px" title="{{ tip }}{% if m.total > 1 %} — latest: {{ m.title }}{% endif %}">
        <span class="kh-u-sr-only">{{ m.longLabel }}: {{ m.total }}{{ ' entry' if m.total == 1 else ' entries' }}. Latest: {{ m.title }}.</span>
      </a>
      {%- else %}
      <span class="kh-timeline__mark kh-timeline__mark--empty" title="{{ m.longLabel }} — no entries">
        <span class="kh-u-sr-only">{{ m.longLabel }}: no entries.</span>
      </span>
      {%- endif %}
      <span class="kh-timeline__year" aria-hidden="true">{{ m.year }}</span>
    </li>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
  <p class="kh-u-sr-only">Range: {{ pulse[0].label }} to {{ (pulse | last).label }}.</p>
</nav>
<span id="kh-after-timeline" tabindex="-1"></span>
{%- endif -%}
